le":"present"},{"entity_id":"mm-simba","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[41,42]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Bafwagbogbo secteur (Bafwagbogbo HZ: Bavadili, Bomili, Bafwaseba, Bafwazio, Singamwambe, Bafwambongo, Bafwangobi, Bavandomo, Bafwangbogo, Bafwagamia) on the Bafwasende-Banalia/Wamba side","evidence":"Northern secteur with artisanal gold-mining zones (e.g. around Bomili) where FARDC/police are posted near mining sites and armed bandits/Mai-Mai Simba elements have occasionally been reported; no known armed-group territorial control. Not verified against 2026 reporting: web research was unavailable for this run (search budget exhausted, search engines and news sites egress-blocked).","unit":"CD5111-bafwasende","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"mm-simba","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[41,42]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Bafwasende secteur villages along the RN4 west and east of the town (Belika, Bafwabalinga, Boyulu, Bafwazana, Bafwandambo, Bafwabianga health areas) and Pumuzika (Tshopo HZ)","evidence":"Roadside villages on the Kisangani-Bafwasende RN4 with state police/administration and no known armed-group control; banditry and poaching occur in the forest. Not verified against 2026 reporting: web research was unavailable for this run (search budget exhausted, search engines and news sites egress-blocked).","unit":"CD5111-bafwasende","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","source_ids":[41]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"low","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Eastern Bafwasende secteur toward Nia-Nia and the Ituri border (Bafwanduo health area: Bafwanduo, Avakubi, PK 300 Badumbu)","evidence":"Villages on the RN4 and Ituri river (Avakubi) near the Mambasa/Okapi reserve border, an area where Mai-Mai Simba poacher/gold-mining groups have historically raided mining sites; no report known of armed-group administration of the villages. Not verified against 2026 reporting: web research was unavailable for this run (search budget exhausted, search engines and news sites egress-blocked).","unit":"CD5111-bafwasende","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"mm-simba","role":"raiding"}],"source_ids":[41,42]},{"controller_id":"cod-pnc","sovereign_id":"cod","status":"dominant","confidence":"medium","basis":"default_state_presence","as_of":"2026-10-01","zone":"Bafwasende town (territorial seat on the RN4 Kisangani-Nia-Nia road, Kenge health area)","evidence":"Chief-town of the territory with territorial administration, PNC commissariat and FARDC elements; Mai-Mai Simba bands active in the surrounding forests and mining areas have not been reported holding the town. Not verified against 2026 reporting: web research was unavailable for this run (search budget exhausted, search engines and news sites egress-blocked).","unit":"CD5111-bafwasende","run_id":"drc-swarm-1","presence":[{"entity_id":"cod-fardc","role":"present"}],"source_ids":[41,42]}],"sources":{"41":{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bafwasende_Territory","title":"Bafwasende Territory","publisher":"Wikipedia"},"42":{"url":"https://www.radiookapi.net/tags/bafwasende","title":"Bafwasende (tag page: Mai-Mai Simba and mining insecurity coverage)","publisher":"Radio Okapi"}},"units":{"CD5111-bafwasende":"Bafwasende territory (Tshopo) lies on the RN4 between Kisangani and Nia-Nia, a forest and artisanal gold-mining area away from the main eastern frontlines. No armed group is known to hold or administer any town as of 2026; the PNC is assessed as controller of Bafwasende town and the secteurs of Bafwasende, Bafwagbogbo and Opienge, with FARDC detachments at the chief-town and around mining areas. Mai-Mai Simba poacher/miner groups operating from the Okapi reserve and Maiko park forests raid mining sites and villages, especially in the east (Avakubi/Bafwanduo) and in Opienge secteur. Web research was unavailable for this run, so confidence is medium for the town and low elsewhere."}}